Can you test these explanations rather than choosing one at the start?
- cash access degrades before account servicing
- manual workarounds create later reconciliation breaks
- recovery restores authorisation before posting catches up

The decision is the order in which critical services should be recovered and =
tested. Please give us a model-ready table, data dictionary and an honest bas=
eline.

You should be able to build the evidence from transaction-level timestamps, c=
hannels, amounts, statuses and error context; ATM attempts, host responses, P=
IN attempts, blocked-card state and latency; customer contacts, complaints an=
d suggestions; debit-order mandates, collection dates, suspensions and cancel=
